      {
        "id": "tnib-b008",
        "slug": "dev-server-memory-leak",
        "path": "data/tnib-b008--dev-server-memory-leak.md",
        "version": 1,
        "title": "Memory leak in development server after hot reload",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "type": "bug",
        "priority": "critical",
        "estimate": "s",
        "created_at": "2026-03-22T09:00:00Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-03-25T14:00:00Z",
        "body": "\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Start development server with `npm run dev`\n2. Make 20+ file changes triggering hot reload\n3. Observe Node.js memory usage climbing from ~150MB to 1.2GB+\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n**Expected:** Memory usage stable around 200-300MB regardless of hot reloads\n**Actual:** Memory grows ~50MB per hot reload and is never reclaimed\n\n## Root Cause\n\nVite's HMR is not cleaning up old module instances. Likely related to circular dependency in the state management layer preventing garbage collection. Investigating with `--inspect` heap snapshots.",
        "order": "n",
        "etag": "5d866a72702271c2"
      },
      {
        "id": "tnib-b012",
        "slug": "search-stale-after-delete",
        "path": "data/tnib-b012--search-stale-after-delete.md",
        "version": 1,
        "title": "Search results not updating after task deletion",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "type": "bug",
        "priority": "normal",
        "estimate": "s",
        "created_at": "2026-03-20T14:00:00Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-03-25T11:00:00Z",
        "body": "\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Create a task with title \"quarterly review\"\n2. Delete the task\n3. Search for \"quarterly\" — deleted task still appears in results\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n**Expected:** Deleted tasks excluded from search results immediately\n**Actual:** Search index retains deleted tasks until server restart\n\n## Root Cause\n\nDelete handler removes from database but doesn't update the Bleve search index. Need to call `index.Delete(taskID)` in the delete path.",
        "order": "u",
        "etag": "85d1f03dab6f2268"
      },
      {
        "id": "tnib-b009",
        "slug": "flaky-user-service-test",
        "path": "data/tnib-b009--flaky-user-service-test.md",
        "version": 1,
        "title": "Flaky test in user_service_test.go",
        "status": "todo",
        "type": "bug",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimate": "s",
        "created_at": "2026-03-18T09:00:00Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-03-22T10:00:00Z",
        "body": "\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Run `go test ./internal/service/ -count=100`\n2. TestUserService_ConcurrentUpdate fails ~5% of the time\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n**Expected:** Test passes consistently\n**Actual:** Intermittent failure with \"context deadline exceeded\" — race condition in test setup\n\n## Root Cause\n\nTest uses a shared database connection pool without proper per-test isolation. When tests run in parallel, the pool is exhausted and some tests timeout waiting for a connection. Need to use `t.Parallel()` with per-test transactions.",
        "order": "o",
        "etag": "2db65ab9890d4a9c"
      },
      {
        "id": "tnib-b010",
        "slug": "safari-grid-layout",
        "path": "data/tnib-b010--safari-grid-layout.md",
        "version": 1,
        "title": "CSS grid layout breaks on Safari 15",
        "status": "todo",
        "type": "bug",
        "priority": "normal",
        "estimate": "m",
        "tags": [
          "browser-compat"
        ],
        "created_at": "2026-03-15T09:00:00Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-03-20T10:00:00Z",
        "body": "\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Open task board in Safari 15.x\n2. Observe columns overlapping when board has \u003e5 columns\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n**Expected:** Columns sized correctly with horizontal scroll when needed\n**Actual:** Columns overlap because Safari 15 doesn't support `subgrid` — falls back to `auto` sizing\n\n## Root Cause\n\nWe use `grid-template-columns: subgrid` which Safari didn't support until 16.0. Need fallback for Safari 15 using explicit column definitions.",
        "order": "p",
        "etag": "8da65a2be37721e9"
      },
      {
        "id": "tnib-b011",
        "slug": "api-500-malformed-json",
        "path": "data/tnib-b011--api-500-malformed-json.md",
        "version": 1,
        "title": "API returns 500 on malformed JSON body",
        "status": "todo",
        "type": "bug",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimate": "s",
        "created_at": "2026-03-18T10:00:00Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-03-22T09:00:00Z",
        "body": "\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Send POST /api/tasks with body: `{invalid json`\n2. Server returns 500 Internal Server Error\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n**Expected:** 400 Bad Request with message \"Invalid JSON: unexpected character at position 1\"\n**Actual:** 500 Internal Server Error with generic message — json.Decoder error is not caught by error middleware\n\n## Root Cause\n\nError middleware only handles our custom `AppError` type. stdlib `json.SyntaxError` and `json.UnmarshalTypeError` fall through to the default 500 handler. Need to add type switches in the error middleware.",
        "order": "q",
        "etag": "104451c4b47f6808"
      },
      {
        "id": "tnib-b013",
        "slug": "file-upload-special-chars",
        "path": "data/tnib-b013--file-upload-special-chars.md",
        "version": 1,
        "title": "File upload fails for names with special characters",
        "status": "todo",
        "type": "bug",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimate": "s",
        "tags": [
          "i18n"
        ],
        "created_at": "2026-03-20T15:00:00Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-03-22T09:00:00Z",
        "body": "\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Attach a file named `报告_2026年.pdf` to a task\n2. Upload fails with \"Invalid filename\" error\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n**Expected:** File uploaded successfully with Unicode filename preserved\n**Actual:** Filename validation regex `^[a-zA-Z0-9._-]+$` rejects non-ASCII characters\n\n## Root Cause\n\nOverly restrictive filename validation. Should sanitize path separators and null bytes but allow Unicode characters.",
        "order": "v",
        "etag": "fcfa2f5aa6289c0c"
      },
      {
        "id": "tnib-b014",
        "slug": "race-condition-concurrent-updates",
        "path": "data/tnib-b014--race-condition-concurrent-updates.md",
        "version": 1,
        "title": "Race condition in concurrent task updates",
        "status": "todo",
        "type": "bug",
        "priority": "critical",
        "estimate": "l",
        "created_at": "2026-03-22T09:00:00Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-03-25T10:00:00Z",
        "body": "\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Open the same task in two browser tabs\n2. Change status to \"done\" in tab A\n3. Immediately change assignee in tab B (before tab A's change is reflected)\n4. Tab B's update overwrites tab A's status change\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n**Expected:** Optimistic concurrency detects the conflict and prompts user to resolve\n**Actual:** Last write wins — tab B's update silently reverts tab A's status change\n\n## Root Cause\n\nAPI uses PUT (full replace) instead of PATCH (partial update). No ETag/If-Match headers for optimistic concurrency control. Need to implement either:\n1. ETags with If-Match headers (preferred)\n2. Field-level versioning",
        "order": "w",
        "etag": "706971549050e303"
      },
      {
        "id": "tnib-b015",
        "slug": "dropdown-zindex-modal",
        "path": "data/tnib-b015--dropdown-zindex-modal.md",
        "version": 1,
        "title": "Dropdown menu z-index conflict with modal",
        "status": "todo",
        "type": "bug",
        "priority": "normal",
        "estimate": "s",
        "tags": [
          "ux"
        ],
        "created_at": "2026-03-22T10:00:00Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-03-25T09:00:00Z",
        "body": "\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Open the task edit modal\n2. Click the priority dropdown inside the modal\n3. Dropdown renders behind the modal backdrop\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n**Expected:** Dropdown floats above the modal\n**Actual:** Dropdown is clipped by modal's `overflow: hidden` and renders behind the backdrop\n\n## Root Cause\n\nDropdown uses `position: absolute` relative to the modal, which has `overflow: hidden`. Need to portal the dropdown to `document.body` or use Floating UI for proper positioning.",
        "order": "x",
        "etag": "f61a253d881ad808"
      },
